codex
I’m tightening the family rather than merely changing the statistic. The revised instance will use a six-dimensional weighted Boolean cube and the paper’s central-symmetry idea: candidates must select whole complementary pairs. That makes the explicit first-moment constraint automatic for every sampled candidate, while leaving about 601 million legal candidates and only two valid PTE halves. It also keeps a 32-integer native witness under the output cap.
