One more audit correction: a pure translation-size dial would only lengthen the written numbers after centering, so it would not honestly harden the reference search. I’m replacing it with an affine scale bit-length. Both weight bits and scale bits now increase the exact-integer cost, while cube recovery still works directly on the scaled subset sums in the same 127 operations.
