 ## Caveats
 
-The observed 0/200,000 guessing rate is only an upper-resolution sampled density under the declared prior: uniform choice among all 16-of-32 halves. It is not evidence against construction-aware algorithms. In fact, affine-cube reconstruction solves every generated instance quickly on a machine, which is why the family is explicitly Track B. Large integer coefficients—not asymptotic NP-hardness—create the gap between mechanical execution and a no-tool response. The panel did not run an ILP/SMT package or lattice reduction; meet-in-the-middle is the strongest implemented generic exact search, and the construction-specific recovery routine is also measured. Finally, external oracle and G9(b) evidence is absent because of the OpenRouter account limit, so this directory is not submission-ready despite all local gates passing.
+The exact density is with respect to the declared prior: uniform choice of 16 out of the 32 reflection pairs. It does not establish asymptotic hardness or resistance to construction-aware methods; the latter deliberately solves every instance in 127 arithmetic operations. This is why the module declares Track B. The coefficient bit lengths make generic exact arithmetic less comfortable by hand, but the operation cap—not coefficient size—is the reported no-tool measure.
+
+The panel did not independently run LLL, an ILP solver, or an SMT solver because the module is dependency-free; instead it includes a complete exact meet-in-the-middle algorithm for the bounded shipping language, which is stronger than a failed relaxation at this size. A solver that recognizes the complete Boolean cube can recover the answer cheaply. Finally, the OpenRouter account failure means G9(b) and the bare multi-vendor hardening verdict are absent: `selftest_report.json` therefore says `all_passed=false`, and this directory must not be submitted as a completed hard family until those script-owned runs succeed.
