codex
Implemented a native Track B Prouhet–Tarry–Escott generator based on the paper’s definitions, affine invariance, and symmetric solutions ([paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.11429)).

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/gen_2506_11429.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Exact answer density: `2 / 601,080,390 ≈ 3.33e-9`.
- All four attacks failed on 8/8 instances.
- Reference algorithm: 589,914 operations, 8/8 solved.
- Compact structural route: 127 operations, 8/8 solved.
- Shipping answer: 1,023 characters, approximately 256 tokens, 32 atoms.

The result is not submission-ready: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for all bare, hinted, and placebo calls. Consequently G9(b) remains unverified and `all_passed` is correctly `false`. After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare loop and both G9 scratch-directory arms.
