& \quad = [382, 402, 403, 456, 485, 549, 559, 596, 608]^k, \nonumber \\
& \qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad (k = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) \tag*{\eqref{k01234567s610}}
\end{align}

\begin{example}
\label{examplek4}
GPTE with \( k_n = 0 \) and all others \( k < 0 \)
\end{example}
By applying simple arithmetic transformations using \eqref{LCM}, based on solutions for GPTE with \( k_1 = 0 \) and all other exponents \( k > 0 \), we have identified 23 distinct types of ideal non-negative integer solutions of GPTE where \( k_n = 0 \) and all other exponents \( k < 0 \). For example,
