Based on \eqref{equationP1235}, when $P_1$, $P_2$, and $P_5$ take certain values, $P_3$ can take at least two distinct real values only if $P_1^2 + P_2 = 0$. However, this is impossible because $P_1^2 + P_2 = 0$ implies that both $P_1$ and $P_2$ must be zero, which contradicts the non-trivial nature of the solution. Therefore, \eqref{equationh125} has no non-trivial real number solution.
