Based on \eqref{equationP1236}, when $P_1$, $P_2$, and $P_6$ take certain values, $P_3$ can take at most two distinct real values. Therefore, $j = 2$. Consequently, there is no ideal solution chain of length $j \geq 3$ for the type $(h = 1, 2, 6)$.
