codex
Implemented a viable Track B Prouhet–Tarry–Escott generator based on the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.11429).

Local verification passes all gates:

- Exact shipping density: 2 / 601,080,390
- Reference meet-in-the-middle: 589,914 operations, 3.581075 s maximum
- Compact Boolean-cube route: 127 operations
- Random guesses: 0 / 200,000
- Four adversarial attacks: 0 / 8 successes each
- Answer size: 1,023 characters, 32 atoms

Deliverables:

- [gen_2506_11429.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/gen_2506_11429.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.11429/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

STEP 4 remains externally blocked: all three hardening runs received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key total limit exceeded” before any oracle answered. The authentic error transcripts are preserved, `.meta.json` has no fabricated verdict, and the claim remains `in_progress`. After increasing the OpenRouter key limit, rerun the bare, structural, and placebo harness commands described in the README.
